    "description": "Five issues found while tracing _SLC - After Save - Player, DRA and Sign Up_ end to end. None block current testing; all are real. Listed worst first.\n\n1. **Duplicate short-circuit may never fire.** Decision `Check_if_has_Duplicate` reads `Has_Duplicates`, but the Boolean variable is declared `hasDuplicates`. `Has_Duplicates` is only an outcome name inside the `Player_Found` decision, which is not a referenceable resource. If it does not resolve, duplicate cases fall through to `Get_DRA` instead of routing to Review Required. **Verify in the org first** — this one may be a red herring if the builder resolved it differently.\n\n1. `Get_DRA` **can run with blank inputs.** `Rep__c EqualTo ''` matches DRAs with a _null_ Rep — which is exactly what a failed rep resolution produces. A click could attach to the wrong assignment. Needs a guard.\n\n1. **No fault connectors anywhere in the flow.** Any DML or query error surfaces as an unhandled flow fault on the SLC insert rather than a Review Required record. The CMS sees a failure it cannot interpret.\n\n1. **Wrong variable in a lookup.** `Update_Sign_Up_with_Reason` writes `varDealRepAsignmentId` into `Related_Deal__c`; the success path writes `varDRArecord.Deal__c`. A DRA Id is landing in a Deal lookup.\n\n1. **Ended assignments still create Sign-Ups.** `Get_DRA` does not filter on `Assignment_Status__c`, so a click against an Ended assignment produces a live Sign-Up. May be intended — worth an explicit decision either way.\n\n_Note: variable name_ `varDealRepAsignmentId` _is misspelled throughout. Cosmetic, but rename it if the flow is opened for any of the above._",
